/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/src/lean/lake/Lake/Config/Package.lean-290-  Artifacts (i.e., build products) of packages will be shared across
/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/src/lean/lake/Lake/Config/Package.lean-291-  local copies by storing them in a cache associated with the Lean toolchain.
/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/src/lean/lake/Lake/Config/Package.lean-292-  This can significantly reduce initial build times and disk space usage when
/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/src/lean/lake/Lake/Config/Package.lean-293-  working with multiple copies of large projects or large dependencies.
/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/src/lean/lake/Lake/Config/Package.lean-294-
/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/src/lean/lake/Lake/Config/Package.lean-295-  As a caveat, build targets which support the artifact cache will not be stored
/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/src/lean/lake/Lake/Config/Package.lean-296-  in their usual location within the build directory. Thus, projects with custom build
/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/src/lean/lake/Lake/Config/Package.lean-297-  scripts that rely on specific location of artifacts may wish to disable this feature.
